  {
   "title": "Small corpus",
   "text": "9.9 million words, versus hundreds of millions for the main languages. Frequency values are unreliable, so there are no frequency bands, only the all-words generators. The reference lexicon has 64,318 words, so generators, neighbourhood measures and cluster filters are rougher than for the main languages."
  },
  {
   "title": "Newspaper vocabulary added",
   "text": "57,118 of the reference words come from a newspaper corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, urd_newscrawl_2016_1M, 26.0 million words); 7,200 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words. Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abjad: CV is orthographic",
   "text": "Urdu is written without short vowels. CV here is orthographic: alif, waw, ye and bari ye (ا آ و ی ے) count as V; the aspiration marker (ھ) and nun ghunna (ں) are modifiers. Diacritics were removed."
  }
 ],
